      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly common to feel this way as we gain self-awareness and realize that \"average\" is a vast and often comfortable place. The pain of giving up on \"destiny\" can be jarring, but it often marks the beginning of a more peaceful acceptance of who you actually are. Instead of viewing this \"middle ground\" as pointless, try to see it as a rare freedom to be exactly as you are without a massive external escape.",
